 incorrectly), i.e. paths = incoming-paths * 2. → test: diamond grid where the converging cell is itself a `^`.\n- [ ] No splitters at all but multiple `.`/`S` cells: beam goes straight down, `countBeamPaths` = 1n regardless of grid width.\n- [ ] `countBeamPaths` returns a `bigint`, not a `number`, even for trivial 1-path grids (`typeof result === 'bigint'`).\n- [ ] Large grid performance: 200x200 grid with 50 splitters arranged to maximize path explosion completes both `countBeamCells` and `countBeamPaths` in well under 5 seconds (test asserts wall-clock time).\n- [ ] Large path counts exceed `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` correctly represented as `bigint` without precision loss (e.g. construct a grid forcing exactly `2n ** 40n` paths and assert exact equality).\n- [ ] `countBeamCells` and `countBeamPaths` do not mutate the input grid.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nAll boxes above checked, `npm test`, `npm run build`, and `npm run lint` all pass cleanly.","new_string":"## Behaviors and verification\n\n- [x] Single straight beam, no splitters: beam travels straight down from `S` to bottom row, visiting one cell per row. → test: `countBeamCells` equals number of rows; `countBeamPaths` equals `1n`.\n- [x] Beam exits immediately when source is on the bottom row (1-row grid). → test: `countBeamCells` = 1, `countBeamPaths` = 1n.\n- [x] Single splitter mid-grid (TASK.md example 1): grid 4x5, `S` at (0,1), `^` at (2,1). → test: `countBeamCells` = 5, `countBeamPaths` = 2n.\n- [x] Two splitters with one branch absorbed off the left edge (TASK.md example 2): grid 4x5, `S` at (0,1), `^` at (1,1),(2,0),(2,2). → test: `countBeamCells` = 6, `countBeamPaths` = 4n.\n- [x] Splitter on the grid edge: a down-left or down-right branch immediately exits the grid (col-1 < 0 or col+1 >= cols) without creating a cell. → test: splitter at column 0 sends only the down-right branch into the grid; down-left branch is absorbed and contributes a path but no visited cell.\n- [x] Splitter on the last row